    "result": "The frai-core suite passes now: all 28 tests in 8 files, up from 2 failing. I changed only source files. No test files were edited, skipped or deleted, and every existing export still works.\n\n**1. Governance test: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` came back `undefined`** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\nThe module imported the schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `RISK_LEVELS`, etc.) but only attached them to its default export. The test imports them by name, so it got nothing. I added named re-exports for them and `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, and left the default export as it was.\n\n**2. Eval test: toxicity score was 0 instead of 1** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n`runEvaluations` calls every metric as `metric(outputs, references)`, but the second parameter of `toxicityMetric` is the list of banned terms. The references (`'hello'`, `'friendly world'`) were being used as banned words, so every output was flagged. In the default metrics list, toxicity now gets only the outputs. Calling `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` directly works as before.\n\nOne small side effect: in `DEFAULT_METRICS`, the toxicity entry is now a wrapper rather than `toxicityMetric` itself. That only matters if some code compares entries to that function by identity. Nothing in the repo does.",
